      "content": "Ah, no worries! I was just about to say that this supplier might be a bit like a **goblin** who keeps stealing your shiny coins (profits) whenever you aren't looking.\n\nJust to recap, I was suggesting that you treat them like a **goblin merchant** who tries to trick you into signing a deal that looks good on paper but has hidden clauses that will eat your budget alive.\n\nHere is the full, uncut checklist to keep those goblins at bay:\n\n1.  **Price Stability Clause**: Prevents the supplier from acting like a **goblin** who suddenly demands more gold (money) for the same goods without a valid reason.\n2.  **Force Majeure**: Protects you if the **goblins** (or nature) actually cause a real disruption, ensuring they can't use it as an excuse to stop delivering.\n3.  **Termination for Convenience**: Gives you the power to kick the **goblins** out of the warehouse if they start behaving badly.\n4.  **Dispute Resolution**: Ensures that if the **goblins** start fighting over who gets the shiny rocks, you get to decide the outcome in your favor.\n\nGood",
